{"name":"Verbena","hex":"#f1dfdf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Verbena","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Verbenaceae – the vervains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Verbena"}],"entries":[{"title":"Verbena","blocks":[{"text":"Verbena, also known as vervain or verveine, is a genus in the family Verbenaceae. It contains about 150 species of annual and perennial herbaceous or semi-woody flowering plants. The majority of the species are native to the Americas and Asia; however, Verbena officinalis, the common vervain or common verbena, is the type species and native to Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Eisenkraut%2C_Passau.JPG/330px-Eisenkraut%2C_Passau.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbena"},{"title":"Verbena (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Verbena was an American rock band from Birmingham, Alabama, founded in the early 1990s by Scott Bondy, Anne Marie Griffin, Les Nuby, and Daniel Johnston. They released three albums, one of which was issued on Merge Records and two of which were issued on Capitol Records."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbena_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Verbena_officinalis_Sturm22.jpg/500px-Verbena_officinalis_Sturm22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Verbena_officinalis_Sturm22.jpg/500px-Verbena_officinalis_Sturm22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Botanical illustration of common vervain (V. officinalis) from Deutschlands Flora in Abbildungen by Johann Georg Sturm and Jacob Sturm, 1796","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVerbena_officinalis_Sturm22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi